  m_Name: JetEngineData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Jet Engine
  engineDescription: "A Jet Engine is a reaction engine that generates thrust by
    drawing in air, compressing it, mixing it with fuel, and igniting the mixture
    to produce high-speed exhaust gases. It operates mainly according to the Brayton
    cycle, consisting of air intake, compression, combustion, and exhaust, with the
    resulting thrust produced according to Newton\u2019s Third Law of Motion. Its
    major components include the air inlet, compressor, combustion chamber, turbine,
    fuel injection system, exhaust nozzle, and shaft. During operation, air is compressed
    to increase its pressure and temperature, after which fuel is injected and burned
    in the combustion chamber. The high-temperature gases expand through the turbine,
    which drives the compressor, and then pass through the exhaust nozzle at high
    velocity to generate thrust. Jet engines are widely used in commercial aircraft,
    military aircraft, and aerospace propulsion systems. From an engineering perspective,
    compressor and turbine efficiency, pressure ratio, combustion stability, fuel
    consumption, thermal loading, and exhaust velocity are important factors affecting
    overall engine performance."
  engineCategory: Engineering
